<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Juvénal Habyarimana</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1937–1994</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Juvénal Habyarimana was a Rwandan army officer who seized power in a coup in 1973 and ruled a one-party state for over twenty years. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rwandan-patriotic-front">Rwandan Patriotic Front</a> invaded in 1990, and he signed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arusha">Arusha</a> Accords in 1993. The shooting down of his plane over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kigali">Kigali</a> on 6 April 1994 was followed within hours by the start of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genocide">genocide</a> against the Tutsi.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/juvenal-habyarimana.jpg" alt="Juvénal Habyarimana" width="320" height="450" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: DF-SC-83-02204.jpg: Templeton derivative work: César (talk) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Juv%C3%A9nal_Habyarimana_(1980).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
